@startuml state-application-status
title State Machine - Application.status lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

[*] --> pending : ApplyJob (POST /applicant/apply/:jobId)

state "Status != approved" as NotApproved {
  state pending
  state shortlisted
  state exam
  state interview
  state rejected
}
state approved

note right of NotApproved
  UpdateApplicationStatus (PATCH /company/candidates/status/:id)
  accepts any of the six values from any current value.
  The code enforces NO ordering (e.g. pending -> approved is allowed).
  Each real change appends {status, changedAt} to statusHistory;
  setting the same status again changes nothing.
end note

NotApproved --> approved : company sets "approved"
approved --> NotApproved : company sets another status
NotApproved --> NotApproved : company sets another non-approved status

NotApproved --> [*] : applicant WithdrawApplication\n[status != approved] / delete resume + document
approved --> [*] : company DeleteCandidate / delete resume + document
NotApproved --> [*] : company DeleteCandidate
NotApproved --> [*] : cascade: Job, company or applicant deleted
approved --> [*] : cascade: Job, company or applicant deleted

note bottom of approved
  Explicitly enforced prohibition: applicant withdrawal of an
  approved application returns 400
  "You can't withdraw an approved application."
end note
@enduml
